insert into public.legal_documents(doc_key, locale, version, title, body, audience, sort_order, status)
values ('terms', 'en', 1, $T$General Terms of Use$T$, $LEGAL$**English - Version 1.0 | Effective upon approved publication**
1. LINKUP is a software platform connecting online merchants, creators and agencies for collaborations, attribution and commissions. It is operated by maayan shpergel, Israeli registered dealer 037093390, also trading as heleni jewelry. LINKUP is a brand, not a limited company, merchant of record or seller to end customers.
2. Users must have legal capacity, provide accurate information, accept applicable role-specific terms and be authorized to act for represented businesses. Accounts may not be transferred without approval.
3. Merchants are responsible for products, prices, inventory, fulfillment, returns, consumer protection, customer service and their taxes. Creators are responsible for truthful advertising, sponsorship disclosures, rights clearance and their taxes. Agencies are responsible for their authority and represented parties.
4. Fraudulent referrals, artificial orders, coupon abuse, unlawful content and unauthorized access are prohibited. Reasonable investigation and proportionate measures may follow, with an opportunity to respond where practicable.
5. The service relies on WooCommerce and third-party data and may experience delays or outages. No sales, earnings or uninterrupted uptime are guaranteed. Reported errors will be assessed reasonably.
6. The operator retains rights in the platform and brand. Users retain rights in their content and grant a limited service-operation license, warranting necessary third-party permissions.
7. Charges are governed by the Commercial Terms for Merchants and the Commissions, Payments and Reconciliation Policy. LINKUP fees are separate from creator commissions and VAT is added to LINKUP service fees.
8. Increases in standard rates require at least 30 days' notice and express acceptance before the increased rate applies. Refusal may prevent new future activity, but cannot extinguish accrued rights. Silence is not consent.
9. Notices use provided contact channels and reasonably documented delivery, subject to challenges of receipt.
10. Material breaches, security risks and unpaid undisputed amounts may lead to proportionate suspension following notice and cure opportunity where feasible. Historical rights and records remain intact. Users may stop future activity subject to legal retention and outstanding duties.
11. Liability remains subject to mandatory law, including liability that cannot lawfully be excluded. Parties should first attempt good-faith resolution through the website form or email. Israeli law applies subject to mandatory jurisdiction and consumer/privacy rules.
12. The Privacy Policy and Cookies and Sales Attribution Policy govern data transparency. Material changes will be notified as legally required, without retroactive impairment of vested rights.$LEGAL$, 'all', 10, 'draft')
on conflict (doc_key, locale, version) do nothing;
